      "content": "It's incredibly brave of you to acknowledge your feelings and show concern for their well-being. While your concern shows compassion, creating more distance from your family might not actually help them heal. The idea that one's self-worth is tied to their family's happiness can be a heavy burden to carry. It could be useful to speak with a professional who can help you work through these feelings. They can offer guidance on achieving self-fulfillment and understanding that your happiness and theirs are not mutually exclusive. Remember, you are not defined by your family, and setting boundaries doesn't absolve you from being good people, but it does mean you care enough to do what's best for everyone involved, including yourself. I remain here to support you through these challenging feelings.",
